    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 4 USER]\ne030\tThat sounds clean on paper.\ne031\tIn reality, Northline has tolerated us being less clean than that.\ne032\tThey let us patch things manually, and we have sometimes built small exceptions because that is how we kept learning.\ne033\tIf I suddenly arrive with a formal evaluation boundary, it could feel like we have become bureaucratic just when they need us.\ne034\tI do not want process language to replace the fact that they helped us get here.\n[Turn 4 ASSISTANT]\ne035\tYou do not need to present a governance ceremony.\ne036\tThe substance can be human: acknowledge what they have contributed, explain that you are genuinely interested, and be honest that the team has other promises and reliability debt.\ne037\tThe boundary can live in your internal plan and in a plain sentence to them.\ne038\tSomething like, “We want to understand this properly, but I do not want our curiosity to sound like a delivery promise.”\ne039\tThat preserves gratitude without converting gratitude into unlimited scope.",
